From: dasher@netcom.com (Anton Sherwood)
Date: Sun, 1 May 1994 23:44:22 -0700
Subject: [#94-5-12] filtering the flood

Here's a wild idea for filtering the List.  I've mentioned
something similar to Sasha, and in News once or twice, but
I don't think I've brought it up here.

Let each user be represented by a point in n-space.  (I think
8 degrees of freedom should be plenty.)  Initially the points
are random.

When A rates a message of B's positively, A moves toward B, and
conversely.  (The points should be normalized from time to time,
so they don't converge to a point or diverge to infinity; perhaps
constrain them to the surface of a hypersphere?)

Each user specifies a tolerance volume; messages written by users
outside that volume are not read.  The volume may be a sphere or
an infinite cone.

Comments?

