We had a thread going a while back on N-dimensional voting theory which is
more or less what you describe.  I think it's a great idea with
applications beyond lists such as this one. 

When I was a business consultant I once proposed this kind of filtering for
video rentals. I love to see widespread use of this kind of filtering for
books, concerts, even friends.

There is a problem however that has to do with the initial position of new
messages (or books, movies, whatever). We want new posts immeadiately but
there is no history to place it in N-space. All the theories I know of for
placing new objects in N-space boil down to someone taking a guess.

A bad initial guess could make all the interrested readers' filters
elliminate the message. Yet there is no way to accurately place the message
in N-space without some population reading it first. 

IMHO the  list population is probably too small to do justice to this type
of filtering  (I'd love to be wrong if somebody can show me how).


