Subject: [#94-5-20] Arabic etymology

Tim Starr, who knows little math and less ling,
makes a pardonable lapse:
> "Algebra" itself is named for the Moslem who discovered it.

"Algebra" comes from an Arabic word that also means something
like "setting a broken bone", i.e. straightening up what is
not straight.

Tim is thinking of "algorithm", formerly "algorism" (but probably
subjected to folk-etymology on the model of "arithmetic"), from
abu-Ja`far Mohammed ibn-Musa al-Khowarizmi.

